### Phase 2 account APIs (/api/users/{userId}/**). See docs/05-security-and-accounts.md.
### Identity is currently the DEV header seam (HeaderUserIdentityResolver):
### every request must carry X-Insurly-User. This is replaced by a JWT before
### anything ships. Roles are app-owned (user_role table): the FIRST request
### for a given user bootstraps its roles from X-Insurly-Roles; after that,
### the header is ignored and only PUT /api/admin/users/{id} can change them.

### Variables
@base = http://localhost:5001/api
@me = {{base}}/users/me
@user = alice
@carId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@addressId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@licenseId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@quoteId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@guestToken = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- profile

### My profile (JIT-creates the app_user row on first call)
GET {{me}}
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}
X-Insurly-Email: alice@example.com
X-Insurly-Name: Alice Example

### Missing identity -> 401
GET {{me}}
Accept: application/json

### Edit my profile (name + date of birth used for quote prefill)
PUT {{me}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

{
  "displayName": "Alice Example",
  "firstName": "Alice",
  "lastName": "Example",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-03-14"
}

### A partly-filled quote payload from held data (profile + latest car + latest licence)
GET {{me}}/quotes/prefill
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- cars

### Car template (blank + _metadata)
GET {{me}}/cars/template
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

### Add a car
POST {{me}}/cars
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

{
  "make": "Toyota",
  "model": "Corolla",
  "year": 2019,
  "vin": "JT2BF22K1W0123456",
  "primaryUse": "COMMUTE",
  "nickname": "Daily"
}

### List my cars
GET {{me}}/cars
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

### One car
GET {{me}}/cars/{{carId}}
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

### Update
PUT {{me}}/cars/{{carId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

{
  "make": "Toyota",
  "model": "Corolla Hybrid",
  "year": 2021,
  "primaryUse": "PLEASURE",
  "nickname": "Weekend"
}

### Another user cannot see it -> 404
GET {{me}}/cars/{{carId}}
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: mallory

### Delete
DELETE {{me}}/cars/{{carId}}
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- addresses

### Add an address (primary)
POST {{me}}/addresses
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

{
  "label": "Home",
  "line1": "12 Baker Street",
  "city": "London",
  "region": "Greater London",
  "postalCode": "NW1 6XE",
  "countryCode": "GB",
  "primary": true
}

### List
GET {{me}}/addresses
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

### Update
PUT {{me}}/addresses/{{addressId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

{
  "label": "Home",
  "line1": "12 Baker Street",
  "line2": "Flat 2",
  "city": "London",
  "postalCode": "NW1 6XE",
  "countryCode": "GB",
  "primary": true
}

### Delete
DELETE {{me}}/addresses/{{addressId}}
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- phones

### Add a phone
POST {{me}}/phones
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

{
  "label": "Mobile",
  "number": "+44 7700 900123",
  "primary": true
}

### List
GET {{me}}/phones
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

### Delete
DELETE {{me}}/phones/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- licences

### Add a licence (number stored encrypted, returned masked)
POST {{me}}/licenses
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

{
  "licenseNumber": "EXAMP123456AB7CD",
  "status": "VALID",
  "issuingRegion": "DVLA",
  "issuedOn": "2015-06-01",
  "expiresOn": "2035-06-01",
  "yearsHeld": 10
}

### List (masked)
GET {{me}}/licenses
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

### One (full number)
GET {{me}}/licenses/{{licenseId}}
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

### Delete
DELETE {{me}}/licenses/{{licenseId}}
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- quotes

### My quotes (a POST /api/quotes/car made with X-Insurly-User set is stamped;
### stamping is wired in step 5 of the rollout — until then, use claim below)
GET {{me}}/quotes
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

### One of my quotes
GET {{me}}/quotes/{{quoteId}}
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

### Claim a guest quote (id + guestToken from POST /api/quotes/car)
POST {{me}}/quotes/claim
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

{
  "quoteId": "{{quoteId}}",
  "guestToken": "{{guestToken}}"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- account

### Delete my account (cascades cars/addresses/licences; quotes -> guest)
DELETE {{me}}
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

###

### ================================================================
### ADMIN-ON-BEHALF-OF  (/api/users/{userId}/**, {userId} = a real user id)
### Any authenticated user's own data uses "me" above; an admin can reach
### the same endpoints for ANY user by id — self-or-admin, via @PreAuthorize.
### ================================================================
@onBehalf = {{base}}/users/{{custId}}
@custId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Non-owner, non-admin -> 403
GET {{onBehalf}}/cars
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

### Add a car to another user's account (requires the ADMIN role)
POST {{onBehalf}}/cars
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: boss
X-Insurly-Roles: admin

{ "make": "Toyota", "model": "Corolla", "year": 2019, "primaryUse": "COMMUTE" }

### Prefill for a quote-on-behalf
GET {{onBehalf}}/quotes/prefill
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: boss
X-Insurly-Roles: admin

### Generate a quote on the customer's behalf
POST {{onBehalf}}/quotes
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: boss
X-Insurly-Roles: admin

{
  "driver":   { "firstName": "Jordan", "lastName": "Rivera", "dateOfBirth": "1990-03-14", "yearsLicensed": 10, "licenseStatus": "VALID" },
  "vehicle":  { "make": "Toyota", "model": "Corolla", "year": 2019, "primaryUse": "COMMUTE" },
  "history":  { "accidentsLast5Years": 0, "violationsLast5Years": 1 },
  "coverage": { "liabilityLimit": "50/100/50", "collision": true, "comprehensive": true, "deductible": 500 }
}

### Their quotes
GET {{onBehalf}}/quotes
Accept: application/json
X-Insurly-User: boss
X-Insurly-Roles: admin

###

### ================================================================
### ADMIN CONSOLE  (/api/admin/**)  — every call needs the admin role.
### Customer records, roles, providers, settings, and the dashboard.
### ================================================================
@admin = http://localhost:5001/api/admin
@adminHdrs = X-Insurly-User: boss

### Non-admin -> 403
GET {{admin}}/dashboard
X-Insurly-User: {{user}}

### Dashboard (totals by status, expiring-soon, user counts, recent feed)
GET {{admin}}/dashboard
Accept: application/json
{{adminHdrs}}
X-Insurly-Roles: admin

### List every customer
GET {{admin}}/users
Accept: application/json
{{adminHdrs}}
X-Insurly-Roles: admin

### Create an admin-managed customer (no email is sent)
POST {{admin}}/users
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
{{adminHdrs}}
X-Insurly-Roles: admin

{
  "email": "jordan@example.com",
  "firstName": "Jordan",
  "lastName": "Rivera",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-03-14"
}

### One customer (with sub-collection counts + links)
GET {{admin}}/users/{{custId}}
Accept: application/json
{{adminHdrs}}
X-Insurly-Roles: admin

### Edit a customer's profile and grant a role (works for self-service too)
PUT {{admin}}/users/{{custId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
{{adminHdrs}}
X-Insurly-Roles: admin

{
  "email": "jordan@example.com",
  "firstName": "Jordan",
  "lastName": "Rivera",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-03-14",
  "roles": ["SALES_ADMIN"]
}

###

### ---------------------------------------------------- system settings
### Public read (no auth) — the frontend uses this to format amounts / dates.
GET {{base}}/system-settings
Accept: application/json

### Admin read — same values plus the selectable option lists in _metadata.
GET {{admin}}/system-settings
Accept: application/json
{{adminHdrs}}
X-Insurly-Roles: admin

### Admin update — timezone is any IANA zone id; language / currency are enum names.
PUT {{admin}}/system-settings
Content-Type: application/json
{{adminHdrs}}
X-Insurly-Roles: admin

{
  "timezone": "America/Sao_Paulo",
  "language": "PT_BR",
  "currency": "BRL"
}

###
